 "limitations": [
  "Rents are published per postcode district. A district is large, and within one of them the range is wide. The site shows the published quartiles alongside the median so that range is visible.",
  "Journey times are the median of departures across a 60 minute window on a weekday morning, computed from the published timetable. They do not account for delays, engineering work, or how full the train is.",
  "A district's journey time is the median across the 750m grid cells inside it, weighted by how much housing each contains. One end of a district may be considerably better connected than the other.",
  "Walking at each end is capped at 20 minutes and the whole journey at 120 minutes. Driving and cycling are not modelled.",
  "Rent and journey time are the two things measured here. They are not the only things that decide where somebody wants to live."
 ]
}